{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775379118-Vb5G7G2EDqJt32CHkTSZ","role":"assistant","created":1775379121,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I found the data I need. Looking at the table UST-1, I can see the \"Treasury operating balance\" with \"Federal Reserve banks\" column:\n\nFor October 1981 (1981-Oct.): 3550\nFor November 1981 (1981-Nov.): 3475\n\nThe change from October to November would be:\n3475 - 3550 = -75\n\nSo the change is -75 million dollars (a decrease of 75 million).\n\nLet me verify this is what the question is asking for. The question asks for \"the change in the Federal Reserve banks operating balance in the U.S. Treasury from calendar month October 1981 to November 1981\". \n\nThis would be November value minus October value:\n3475 - 3550 = -75\n\nSince it's asking for the change as a single whole number, and it's a decrease, I should report -75.\n\nWait, let me double check by looking at the page 28 text that was extracted:\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_f82fc154eac9464a9ec672de","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"cat /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1981_12_page_28.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
{"type":"message","message":{"id":"msg_b48f673f-5409-44f0-9409-e6ab5b5d98f1","role":"user","created":1775379121,"content":[{"type":"toolResponse","id":"call_f82fc154eac9464a9ec672de","toolResult":{"status":"success","value":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"14\nTreasury Bulletin\nACCOUNT OF THE U.S. TREASURY\nSource and Availability of the Balance in the Account of the U.S. Treasury\nThe operating cash of the Treasury is maintained in Treasury's accounts with the Federal Reserve banks and branches and in tax loan accounts. As the balances in the accounts at the Federal Reserve Banks become depleted, they are restored by calling in (Withdrawing) funds from thousands of financial institutions throughout the country authorized to maintain tax and loan accounts.\nUnder authority of P.L. 95-147, the Treasury implemented a program on November 2, 1978, to invest a portion of its operating cash in obligations of depositories maintaining tax and loan accounts. Under the Treasury Tax and Loan investment program, depository financial institutions select the manner in which they will participate in the program. Depositaries that wish to retain funds deposited in their tax and loan accounts in interest-bearing obligations participate under the Note Option; depositaries that wish to remit the funds to the Treasury's account at Federal Reserve bank participate under the Remittance Option.\nDeposits to tax and loan accounts occur in the normal course of business under a uniform procedure applicable to all financial institutions whereby customers of financial institutions deposit with them tax payments and funds for the purchase of Government securities. In most cases the transaction involves merely the transfer of funds from a customer's account to the tax and loan account in the same financial institution. On occasions, to the extent authorized by the Treasury, financial institutions are permitted to deposit in these accounts proceeds from subscriptions to public debt securities entered for their own account as well as for the accounts of their customers.\nThe tax and loan system premits the Treasury to collect fund through financial institutions and to leave the funds in Note Option depositaries and in the financial communities in which they arise until such time as the Treasury needs the funds for its operations. In this way the Treasury is able to neutralize the effect of its fluctuation operations on Note Option financial institution reserves and the economy.\nTable UST-1. - Status of the Account of the U.S. Treasury\n(In millions of dollars)\n<table><tr><th rowspan=\"2\">End of fiscal year or month</th><th colspan=\"3\">Treasury operating balance 1/</th><th colspan=\"2\">Funds in process of collection through</th><th colspan=\"5\">Time deposits and other</th></tr><tr><th>Federal Reserve banks</th><th>Treasury tax and loan note accounts</th><th>Other depositaries 2/</th><th>Total 3/</th><th>Federal Reserve</th><th>Other depositaries 4/</th><th>interest-bearing demand accounts</th><th>Other demand accounts 5/</th><th>Coin currency and coinage metal</th><th>Miscellaneous items</th><th>Gold balance 6/</th><th>Balance in account of the U.S. Treasury</th></tr><tr><td>1973</td><td>4,038</td><td>8,433</td><td>106</td><td>12,576</td><td>243</td><td>117</td><td>41</td><td>-</td><td>586</td><td>70</td><td>107</td><td>13,741</td></tr><tr><td>1974</td><td>2,919</td><td>6,152</td><td>88</td><td>9,159</td><td>276</td><td>135</td><td>19</td><td>-</td><td>602</td><td>54</td><td>106</td><td>10,352</td></tr><tr><td>1975</td><td>5,773</td><td>1,475</td><td>343</td><td>7,591</td><td>369</td><td>76</td><td>35</td><td>-</td><td>752</td><td>46</td><td>-</td><td>8,868</td></tr><tr><td>1976</td><td>11,975</td><td>2,854</td><td>7</td><td>14,836</td><td>235</td><td>55</td><td>70</td><td>-</td><td>819</td><td>50</td><td>-</td><td>16,065</td></tr><tr><td>T.Q.</td><td>13,299</td><td>4,119</td><td>-</td><td>17,418</td><td>184</td><td>-18</td><td>195</td><td>-</td><td